# Build-time switches. Expo CLI loads `.env` for every build, a store build included.

# Pro testing in a Release build. "1" shows the "Pro (testing)" switch in Settings → Subscription
# and a "TEST BUILD" label at the bottom of Settings. Expo inlines the value when the JavaScript
# bundle is built, so it is fixed per build. Leave it unset for a production build: the switch is
# then hidden and a stored override is ignored. Safest is to pass it on the command line only:
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_PRO_TESTING=1 npx expo run:ios --configuration Release
EXPO_PUBLIC_PRO_TESTING=
